sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Py as PyTorch
    participant AT as ATen dispatcher
    participant CU as CUDA runtime
    participant Drv as Driver
    participant GPU as GPU
    Py->>AT: torch.matmul(a, b)
    AT->>AT: pick the kernel for this dtype and device
    AT->>CU: cudaLaunchKernel
    CU->>Drv: ioctl with the launch descriptor
    Drv->>GPU: push onto the stream's command queue
    Note over CU,GPU: the call returns immediately — launches are asynchronous
    Py->>Py: Python continues while the GPU works
    Py->>CU: cudaStreamSynchronize or a .cpu() call
    CU->>GPU: wait for completion
    GPU-->>Py: results
    Note over Py,GPU: that sync point is where a "fast" model suddenly shows its real cost
